{% comment %}
  Section contract.
  Home: "The physics of light on skin". Four short, factual notes (photon energy, resonant
  absorption, depth by wavelength, the best-studied absorber in red-light research) on a light
  micrograph. Physics only: no treatment or result claims.
  @example
  <!-- templates/index.json → "sk_science" -->
{% endcomment %}
<section class="hb sci" id="science" aria-labelledby="sci-h">
  {%- if images['hb-sci-glow.png'] -%}{{ images['hb-sci-glow.png'] | image_url: width: 2000 | image_tag: class: 'sci__ph', widths: '800,1200,1600,2000', sizes: '100vw', alt: '', loading: 'lazy' }}{%- endif -%}
  <div class="hb-wrap sci__in">
    <header class="sci__head">
      <p class="sci__k">{{ section.settings.kicker | escape }}</p>
      <h2 class="sci__h" id="sci-h">{{ section.settings.heading | escape }}<br><em>{{ section.settings.heading_em | escape }}</em></h2>
      <p class="sci__lede">{{ section.settings.text | escape }}</p>
    </header>
    <ol class="sci__grid">
      <li class="sci__c">
        <span class="sci__n">01 · Photon</span>
        <b class="sci__d">E = hc/λ</b>
        <p>Light travels in packets of energy, and the wavelength sets how much each one carries. Red at 630 nm: 1.97 eV per photon. Blue at 470 nm: 2.64 eV. Shorter wave, more energy.</p>
      </li>
      
      <li class="sci__c">
        <span class="sci__n">02 · Depth</span>
        <b class="sci__d">470 → 630 nm</b>
        <p>Skin scatters short wavelengths close to the surface; longer ones travel further before they are absorbed. Blue stays in the upper layers. Red goes deeper.</p>
      </li>
      
    </ol>
    <div class="sci__foot">
      <a class="sci__cta" href="/products/lezo-7-color-led-face-mask#hb-colors">Explore the six wavelengths</a>
      <p class="sci__fine">Physics, not promises. LEZO and Booster Pro are cosmetic devices; follow the manual for session time and eye protection. Individual results vary. Background: illustrative micrograph.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
.sci{position:relative;overflow:hidden;isolation:isolate;background:#fbf3f5;color:#1a1012;padding:clamp(64px,9vw,112px) 0;--sci-ac:#c2413a;--sci-ed:"Instrument Serif","Times New Roman",serif}
.sci__ph{position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:right center;z-index:-2}
.sci:before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;z-index:-1;background:linear-gradient(90deg,rgba(251,243,245,.97) 0%,rgba(251,243,245,.85) 45%,rgba(251,243,245,.35) 100%)}
.sci__head{max-width:760px;margin-bottom:clamp(32px,5vw,56px)}
.sci__k{margin:0 0 14px;font:800 15px/1 var(--hb-disp);letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sci-ac)}
.sci__h{margin:0;font:800 clamp(48px,8vw,104px)/.86 var(--hb-disp);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.sci__h em{display:inline-block;margin-top:6px;font:italic 400 clamp(42px,7vw,92px)/.95 var(--sci-ed);text-transform:none;color:var(--sci-ac)}
.sci__lede{margin:22px 0 0;max-width:56ch;font-size:clamp(16px,1.4vw,19px);line-height:1.5;color:#4a3a3e}
.sci__grid{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:12px}
.sci__c{padding:22px 22px 24px;border-radius:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.72);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.9);box-shadow:0 18px 40px -26px rgba(120,40,70,.35);-webkit-backdrop-filter:blur(14px);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
.sci__n{display:block;font:800 13px/1 var(--hb-disp);letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--sci-ac)}
.sci__d{display:block;margin:14px 0 12px;font:800 clamp(30px,3vw,40px)/.95 var(--hb-disp);letter-spacing:-.01em;text-transform:none}
.sci__c p{margin:0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#4a3a3e}
.sci__foot{display:grid;gap:16px;margin-top:clamp(28px,4vw,44px)}
.sci__cta{justify-self:start;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding-bottom:6px;border-bottom:2px solid currentColor;color:#1a1012;text-decoration:none;font:800 18px/1 var(--hb-disp);letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase}
.sci__cta:after{content:"→";font-family:var(--hb-sans);font-weight:500}
.sci__fine{margin:0;max-width:70ch;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;color:#7a666b}
@media(min-width:700px){.sci__grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}
@media(min-width:1100px){.sci__grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:16px}}
</style>
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "HB · The science",
  "settings": [
    {"type": "text", "id": "kicker", "label": "Kicker", "default": "The physics of light on skin"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Why the color"},
    {"type": "text", "id": "heading_em", "label": "Heading (italic line)", "default": "matters."},
    {"type": "textarea", "id": "text", "label": "Intro", "default": "You don’t need a physics degree to use an LED mask, but knowing why the color matters helps you pick the right one. Here is the short version."}
  ],
  "presets": [{"name": "HB · The science"}]
}
{% endschema %}
